$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n use-three-for-b --no-commit [cwd: fix-sum]
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: main is not checked out, so todoer can only commit the pull request on it - check out main, or remove --no-commit

$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n use-three-for-b --todo fix-the-sum [cwd: fix-sum]
submitted use-three-for-b: 1 commit, 3 files, into main
.todoer/prs/use-three-for-b on main
todos: fix-the-sum
committed on main

$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n use-three-for-b [cwd: fix-sum]
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: main already has the pull request use-three-for-b - use -n use-three-for-b --update to replace it, or another -n to make a new pull request

$ git log --format=%s -2 main && git status --short && todoer pr ls
todoer: submit use-three-for-b
todoer: claim fix-the-sum
no open pull requests

$ git switch -q main && todoer pr ls && todoer pr merge use-three-for-b
use-three-for-b  no comments  me@example.com
merged use-three-for-b into main
done: fix-the-sum

$ git log --format=%s -3 && git status --short && todoer ls
todoer: merge use-three-for-b
todoer: submit use-three-for-b
todoer: claim fix-the-sum
no todos

